  "derivation": "Foundation 27 ContentSerializer attributes. Contract rows come from the pinned public metadata and docs/generated/xna-il-inventory.json. Mapping rows encode what the pinned Microsoft.Xna.Framework.dll IL establishes: ContentSerializerAttribute's constructor stores allowNull true before calling the base constructor and leaves every other field at its CLR default; CollectionItemName answers the literal \"Item\" whenever the raw field is null or empty and its setter throws ArgumentNullException for null or empty; HasCollectionItemName is the negation of that same emptiness test; Clone copies the six raw fields; the CollectionItemName and RuntimeType constructors throw ArgumentNullException for null or empty while the TypeVersion constructor validates nothing; and ContentSerializerIgnoreAttribute declares nothing but its constructor. System.Attribute projects to the CNA::Runtime::Attribute marker base and System.ArgumentNullException to Ruby's ArgumentError. None is snapshotted from the cna-ruby implementation.",
